# Posta — shared Docker build-context excludes (T0.7.1)
#
# The build context for all three app images (apps/{api,worker,web}/Dockerfile)
# is the repo root — each Dockerfile's `pruner` stage needs the whole
# workspace to compute a per-app subset via `turbo prune` (T0.7.3). Without
# this file, `docker build` uploads every one of these directories to the
# daemon on EVERY build, which busts the build cache on any file change at
# all (a touched .md file invalidates the same layers as a source change)
# and, for node_modules especially, makes the context multiple GB.

# --- dependencies & build output --------------------------------------------
# Reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image; never useful from the host. A bare
# `node_modules/` only matches a TOP-LEVEL node_modules — Docker's ignore
# patterns are not recursive like .gitignore's, so every one of these needs
# the `**/` prefix to also catch apps/*/node_modules, apps/web/.next, etc.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/.turbo/

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Never bake local credentials into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- vcs & docs --------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
docs/

# --- data files ----------------------------------------------------------
# GeoIP .mmdb files (S0.7, T0.7.9/10 — a later batch): fetched or baked in
# a dedicated step, never picked up implicitly via the build context.
**/*.mmdb
